+Most hooks are fire-and-forget observers. Behavior-changing hooks include context injection, tool policies, model routing, and gateway dispatch controls.
+
+`resolve_model_route` is a policy hook, separate from the observer-only API hooks. A runtime must contain `model`, `provider`, `base_url`, `api_mode`, and `api_key`; it may include `capabilities` and `request_overrides`. Any veto wins; otherwise the first route wins. The agent uses native `switch_model`, retains the frozen system prompt and executed tool results, replaces request overrides, and clears stale provider fallbacks. Return an empty `request_overrides` mapping when leaving a route with custom parameters. Credentials are internal return values and must never be logged. Callback errors and bounded timeouts fail closed. Without a routing policy there is no behavior change. Auxiliary LLM calls are outside this hook.
 
 All callbacks should accept `**kwargs` for forward compatibility. If a hook callback crashes, it's logged and skipped. Other hooks and the agent continue normally.
 
